// Module c-headache: secondary headache red flags (SNNOOP10), giant cell arteritis, idiopathic
// intracranial hypertension, primary headaches by ICHD-3 features (migraine with and without aura,
// tension-type, cluster), trigeminal neuralgia, medication overuse headache, and the principles of
// acute versus preventive treatment. Subarachnoid hemorrhage and cerebral venous thrombosis are taught
// in c-ich-sah and c-cvt-dissection; here they appear only as red-flag destinations. No doses.

