          body: "In one evening the emergency department sees three people with headache. A 31-year-old has had attacks like tonight's since her teens. A 69-year-old has had a new ache over his temple for three weeks and now his jaw hurts when he chews. A 48-year-old felt something burst in her head while lifting a suitcase, and the pain was at its worst within seconds. All three are in pain and two have normal examinations. Only one can safely go home without tests, and the difference is entirely in the history.",
