            mechanism: "Aura is thought to reflect [[cortical-spreading-depression|cortical spreading depression]]: a slow wave of neuronal excitation followed by suppression that creeps slowly across the cortex. A wave crossing visual cortex produces a shimmering edge (excitation) followed by a blind patch (suppression), which is why the disturbance moves and why positive symptoms come first. The headache involves activation of trigeminal nerve fibers around meningeal vessels.",
